IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ica-dates`
IMPORT `ica-core`

-- Civil Liability Act 1936 (SA), Parts 7A and 7B -- the seat of the person abused as a child who brings, or may bring,
-- a claim against an institution (or that person's representative). Every question is asked as that person would ask
-- it; every input is a fact the person can state, or where a court's judgment stands. No rule is restated here: each
-- question calls ica-core.l4.
--
-- Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website, as collected by the Open Australian Legal Corpus on
-- 10 March 2025 (the Act as at 22 June 2023; unofficial, possibly out of date). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for
-- public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `The person abused as a child: claims against institutions`

§§ `Is my claim an abuse claim (Part 7A Division 1)`

-- Situation: you were abused as a child by someone connected with an organisation, school, church, club, care
-- provider or government body that was responsible for you.

@export Is my claim an "abuse claim" against an institution under the Civil Liability Act 1936 (SA) Part 7A (s 50A, s 50C)?
GIVEN `my age when abused` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in completed years when the abuse happened ("child" means under 18)
      `the kind of abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse` @desc The kind of abuse: sexual abuse; serious physical abuse; psychological abuse related to sexual abuse or serious physical abuse; physical abuse that was not serious; psychological abuse not related to those; or another kind of abuse
      `the body was responsible for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation or body (private or public, including government) was responsible for you and provided an activity, program or service of a kind that gives a person an opportunity to have contact with a child
      `the body is a family` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the "body" is in fact a family (a family is not an institution)
      `the abuser's connection` IS A `Connection with the institution` @desc How the person who abused you was connected with the body: its officer, office holder, representative, leader, owner, employee, agent, volunteer or contractor; a minister, religious leader or member of personnel of a religious organisation; the individual to whom it delegated your care, or a person in such a role with the entity it delegated to; a designated carer you were placed with (a foster or kinship carer under the Children and Young People (Safety) Act 2017), who was or was not your parent or guardian; a person connected only with an entity the body funds or regulates; or some other connection
      `I was in its care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the abuse happened while you were under the care, supervision, control or authority of the body
GIVETH AN `Abuse claim answer`
`Is my claim an abuse claim against an institution` MEANS
    `the abuse claim answer for` (`Abuse facts` WITH
        `the age when abused` IS `my age when abused`
        `the abuse` IS `the kind of abuse`
        `the body was responsible for the child and gave contact with children` IS `the body was responsible for me`
        `the body is a family` IS `the body is a family`
        `the abuser's connection` IS `the abuser's connection`
        `the child was under its care, supervision, control or authority` IS `I was in its care`)

@export Was the person who abused me an employee of the institution, or akin to one, for Part 7A of the Civil Liability Act 1936 (SA) (s 50A(1), (2))?
GIVEN `they were its employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person was the institution's employee in the ordinary sense (employed by it)
      `their work was integral to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person carried out activities as an integral part of the activities the institution carried on
      `their work was for its benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person carried out those activities for the institution's benefit
      `it was their own independent business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether those activities were carried out for a recognisably independent business of the person, or of another person or institution
      `they were a designated carer acting as one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether those activities were the activities of a designated carer (a person with whom a child is placed under the Children and Young People (Safety) Act 2017), carried on as a designated carer
GIVETH AN `Employee answer`
`Was the person who abused me an employee of the institution` MEANS
    `the employee answer for` (`Employment facts` WITH
        `an employee in the ordinary sense` IS `they were its employee`
        `the activities were an integral part of the institution's` IS `their work was integral to it`
        `they were for the institution's benefit` IS `their work was for its benefit`
        `they were for a recognisably independent business` IS `it was their own independent business`
        `they were a designated carer's activities as a designated carer` IS `they were a designated carer acting as one`)

§§ `The institution's duty and its vicarious liability (Part 7A Divisions 2 and 3)`

@export Is the institution taken to have breached its duty to take all reasonable steps to prevent the abuse of me as a child (Civil Liability Act 1936 (SA) ss 50D, 50E, 50F)?
GIVEN `my age when abused` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in completed years when the abuse happened ("child" means under 18)
      `the kind of abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse` @desc The kind of abuse: sexual abuse; serious physical abuse; psychological abuse related to sexual abuse or serious physical abuse; physical abuse that was not serious; psychological abuse not related to those; or another kind of abuse
      `the body was responsible for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation or body (private or public, including government) was responsible for you and provided an activity, program or service of a kind that gives a person an opportunity to have contact with a child
      `the body is a family` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the "body" is in fact a family (a family is not an institution)
      `the abuser's connection` IS A `Connection with the institution` @desc How the person who abused you was connected with the institution (as in the abuse claim question)
      `I was in its care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the abuse happened while you were under the care, supervision, control or authority of the institution
      `the day of the abuse` IS A DATE @desc The day the abuse happened (if it happened over a period, ask separately for the part before and the part on or after 1 August 2022)
      `it was wholly unrelated to their role` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the abuse happened in circumstances wholly unrelated to the abuser's connection with the institution
      `my care had been delegated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the institution had delegated your care, supervision, control or authority to another institution, and the abuser was connected with that other institution
      `it was unrelated to either institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your care had been delegated: whether the abuse happened in circumstances wholly unrelated to the abuser's connection with either institution
      `the reasonable steps finding` IS A `Court finding` @desc Where the court stands on whether the institution has proved that it took all reasonable steps to prevent the abuse: found that it proved it; found that it did not; or not decided yet
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
`Is the institution taken to have breached its duty to prevent the abuse` MEANS
    `the duty answer for` (`Duty facts` WITH
        `the abuse facts` IS (`Abuse facts` WITH
            `the age when abused` IS `my age when abused`
            `the abuse` IS `the kind of abuse`
            `the body was responsible for the child and gave contact with children` IS `the body was responsible for me`
            `the body is a family` IS `the body is a family`
            `the abuser's connection` IS `the abuser's connection`
            `the child was under its care, supervision, control or authority` IS `I was in its care`)
        `the day of the abuse` IS `the day of the abuse`
        `wholly unrelated to the abuser's association with the institution` IS `it was wholly unrelated to their role`
        `the care was delegated and the abuser was associated with the delegate` IS `my care had been delegated`
        `wholly unrelated to the abuser's association with either institution` IS `it was unrelated to either institution`
        `the institution proved it took all reasonable steps` IS `the reasonable steps finding`)

@export Is the institution vicariously liable for the abuse of me as a child by its employee (Civil Liability Act 1936 (SA) ss 50D, 50G)?
GIVEN `my age when abused` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in completed years when the abuse happened ("child" means under 18)
      `the kind of abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse` @desc The kind of abuse: sexual abuse; serious physical abuse; psychological abuse related to sexual abuse or serious physical abuse; physical abuse that was not serious; psychological abuse not related to those; or another kind of abuse
      `the body was responsible for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation or body (private or public, including government) was responsible for you and provided an activity, program or service of a kind that gives a person an opportunity to have contact with a child
      `the body is a family` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the "body" is in fact a family (a family is not an institution)
      `I was in its care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the abuse happened while you were under the care, supervision, control or authority of the institution
      `the day of the abuse` IS A DATE @desc The day the abuse happened (if it happened over a period, ask separately for the part before and the part on or after 1 August 2022)
      `they were its employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the abuser was the institution's employee in the ordinary sense (employed by it)
      `their work was integral to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the abuser carried out activities as an integral part of the activities the institution carried on
      `their work was for its benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the abuser carried out those activities for the institution's benefit
      `it was their own independent business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether those activities were carried out for a recognisably independent business of the abuser or of another person or institution
      `they were a designated carer acting as one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether those activities were a designated carer's, carried on as a designated carer
      `the occasion finding` IS A `Court finding` @desc Where the court stands on whether the apparent performance of the role the institution placed the abuser in supplied the occasion for the abuse (taking into account whether the role gave authority, power or control over you, your trust, or the ability to achieve intimacy with you): found that it did; found that it did not; or not decided yet
      `they took advantage of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the abuser took advantage of that occasion to abuse you
GIVETH A `Vicarious answer`
`Is the institution vicariously liable for the abuse by its employee` MEANS
    `the vicarious answer for` (`Vicarious facts` WITH
        -- The abuser's connection is not read by s 50G (an employee is connected anyway): a fixed placeholder.
        `the abuse facts` IS (`Abuse facts` WITH
            `the age when abused` IS `my age when abused`
            `the abuse` IS `the kind of abuse`
            `the body was responsible for the child and gave contact with children` IS `the body was responsible for me`
            `the body is a family` IS `the body is a family`
            `the abuser's connection` IS `an officer, office holder, representative, leader, owner, employee, agent, volunteer or contractor of the institution`
            `the child was under its care, supervision, control or authority` IS `I was in its care`)
        `the employment facts` IS (`Employment facts` WITH
            `an employee in the ordinary sense` IS `they were its employee`
            `the activities were an integral part of the institution's` IS `their work was integral to it`
            `they were for the institution's benefit` IS `their work was for its benefit`
            `they were for a recognisably independent business` IS `it was their own independent business`
            `they were a designated carer's activities as a designated carer` IS `they were a designated carer acting as one`)
        `the day of the abuse` IS `the day of the abuse`
        `the role supplied the occasion` IS `the occasion finding`
        `the employee took advantage of that occasion` IS `they took advantage of it`)

§§ `Whom to sue (Part 7A Division 4)`

-- Situation: the institution was not incorporated when you were abused, or has changed since, or has nominated a
-- defendant. Ask these once you know you have an abuse claim.

@export Whom can I bring my abuse claim against, where the institution was unincorporated, has since incorporated, or has a nominee (Civil Liability Act 1936 (SA) ss 50H, 50I, 50J, 50K, 50S)?
GIVEN `it was incorporated then` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the institution was an incorporated body (a company, incorporated association or other body corporate) when your cause of action accrued
      `it is incorporated now` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the institution is an incorporated body now
      `my claim is against an office holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim is founded on the responsibility, for the institution or for the abuser, of a person who held an office of authority in the institution (for example a bishop, principal or committee member) when your cause of action accrued
      `they still hold that office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that former office holder still holds that office
      `I could sue but for the change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you could maintain proceedings on the claim if nothing had changed (the office holder still in office, or the institution still unincorporated): for example, it has not been finally decided or released
      `it has a nominee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the institution has a nominee, a person who has agreed to be (or a trustee the court has ordered to be) the defendant for abuse claims against it
GIVETH A LIST OF `Defendant route`
`Whom can I bring my abuse claim against` MEANS
    `the routes for` (`Defendant facts` WITH
        `it was incorporated when the cause of action accrued` IS `it was incorporated then`
        `it is incorporated now` IS `it is incorporated now`
        `the claim is against a former office holder` IS `my claim is against an office holder`
        `the former office holder still holds the office` IS `they still hold that office`
        `proceedings could be maintained but for the change` IS `I could sue but for the change`
        `the institution has a nominee` IS `it has a nominee`)

@export The institution has changed, merged or split since I was abused: is today's institution the one that is liable (Civil Liability Act 1936 (SA) s 50R)?
GIVEN `what became of it` IS A `What became of the institution` @desc What became of the institution since your cause of action accrued: it continues (perhaps renamed, restructured, incorporated or working in another area); all or part of it merged into another institution; all or part of it merged with other entities to form a new one; part of it left and the remainder continues; a chain of such changes leads to today's institution; or it ceased with no successor
      `its members are of the same class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the class or type of its members is substantially the same as it was then
      `its purposes are the same` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether its primary purposes or work are substantially the same as they were then
      `the number of successors` IS A NUMBER @desc How many institutions today are successors of the old institution through mergers or as remainders (0 if it continues itself)
GIVETH A `Continuity answer`
`Is today's institution the one that is liable` MEANS
    `the continuity answer for` `what became of it` `members` `its members are of the same class` `purposes` `its purposes are the same` `successors` `the number of successors`

@export A court earlier decided against me because the person or institution was not an appropriate defendant: can I sue again (Civil Liability Act 1936 (SA) s 50U)?
GIVEN `there was such a judgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court gave judgment on your claim on the ground that the person or institution you sued was not an appropriate defendant
      `the day of the judgment` IS A DATE @desc The day that judgment was given (any day if there was none)
      `the leave finding` IS A `Court finding` @desc Where the court stands on your application for leave to commence the new proceedings (granted, being satisfied that it is just and reasonable; refused; or not decided or not yet asked)
GIVETH AN `Earlier judgment answer`
`Can I sue again after an earlier judgment that the defendant was not appropriate` MEANS
    `the earlier judgment answer for` `there was such a judgment` `on` `the day of the judgment` `with leave` `the leave finding`

§§ `Getting paid (Part 7A Divisions 4 and 5)`

-- Situation: you have, or expect, a judgment or settlement against an institution, its nominee or an office holder.

@export Is this trust an "associated trust" of the institution, whose assets can be used to pay my abuse claim (Civil Liability Act 1936 (SA) s 50B)?
GIVEN `the institution uses it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the institution uses the trust to carry out its functions or activities
      `the institution has power over it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the institution has, directly or indirectly, a power to control how the trust's income is applied or its property distributed, to obtain the benefit of its property or income, to appoint or remove a trustee or beneficiary, or to determine any other decision about the trust's operations
      `a member or manager has such power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a member or manager of the institution has such a power under the trust deed
      `the trustee follows its directions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a trustee is accustomed to act, or is formally or informally obliged to act, on the directions, instructions or wishes of the institution or of a member or manager of it
      `there is a nominee order for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court order is in force making the trustee of this trust the institution's nominee for an abuse claim (s 50J(5))
GIVETH A `Trust answer`
`Is this trust an associated trust of the institution` MEANS
    `the trust answer for` (`Trust facts` WITH
        `the institution uses the trust for its functions or activities` IS `the institution uses it`
        `the institution has a power over the trust` IS `the institution has power over it`
        `a member or manager has such a power under the trust deed` IS `a member or manager has such power`
        `the trustee acts on the institution's directions` IS `the trustee follows its directions`
        `a s 50J(5) order is in force for it` IS `there is a nominee order for it`)

@export Out of what assets can my judgment or settlement (and the costs of the proceeding) be paid, and is anyone not personally liable (Civil Liability Act 1936 (SA) ss 50L-50P)?
GIVEN `who is liable to me` IS A `Liable party` @desc Who is liable under your judgment or settlement: the institution; the institution's nominee that is the trustee of an associated trust of the institution; the institution's nominee that is not such a trustee; or the current holder of an office, sued in the name of the office
GIVETH A LIST OF `Asset source`
`Out of what assets can my judgment or settlement be paid` MEANS
    `the assets for` `who is liable to me`

@export Can I ask the court to make the trustee of a trust the defendant (nominee) for my abuse claim against an unincorporated institution, and from when (Civil Liability Act 1936 (SA) s 50J(5), (6))?
GIVEN `it is unincorporated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the institution is an unincorporated body
      `the day I commenced my proceeding` IS A DATE @desc The day you commenced your proceeding for the abuse claim against the institution
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date (or the day you would apply)
      `it has a nominee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the institution already has a nominee
      `the nominee assets finding` IS A `Court finding` @desc If there is a nominee: where the court stands on whether the nominee does not have sufficient assets to meet the liability that may be found on your claim (satisfied; not satisfied; or not decided yet)
      `it is an associated trust now` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the trust is now an associated trust of the institution
      `it used to be one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the trust used to be an associated trust of the institution
      `the avoidance finding` IS A `Court finding` @desc If it is no longer an associated trust: where the court stands on whether a reason for that was to try to keep trust property from being used to meet an abuse claim (satisfied; not satisfied; or not decided yet)
      `the appropriateness finding` IS A `Court finding` @desc Where the court stands on whether the order would be appropriate (satisfied; not satisfied; or not decided yet)
GIVETH A `Nominee order answer`
`Can I ask the court to make a trust's trustee the institution's nominee` MEANS
    `the nominee order answer for` (`Nominee order facts` WITH
        `the institution is unincorporated` IS `it is unincorporated`
        `the day the proceeding was commenced` IS `the day I commenced my proceeding`
        `the day of asking` IS `today`
        `there is a nominee already` IS `it has a nominee`
        `the nominee lacks sufficient assets` IS `the nominee assets finding`
        `the trust is an associated trust now` IS `it is an associated trust now`
        `the trust used to be an associated trust` IS `it used to be one`
        `a reason it ceased was to avoid abuse claims` IS `the avoidance finding`
        `the order would be appropriate` IS `the appropriateness finding`)

@export The court ordered the institution to identify its associated trusts and their financial capacity: by when must it do so (Civil Liability Act 1936 (SA) s 50J(7)(a))?
GIVEN `the day of the order` IS A DATE @desc The day the court made the order
      `the court set another period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court set a period other than 28 days
      `the days the court set` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days the court set (any number if it did not set another period)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must the institution identify its associated trusts` MEANS
    `the day of the order` `plus days` (`the period ordered` `the court set another period` `the days the court set`)

@export Has the institution identified its associated trusts and their financial capacity within the time the court ordered, or is there still time (Civil Liability Act 1936 (SA) s 50J(7)(a))?
GIVEN `the day of the order` IS A DATE @desc The day the court made the order
      `the court set another period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court set a period other than 28 days
      `the days the court set` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days the court set (any number if it did not set another period)
      `it has complied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the institution has identified the trusts and given the information
      `the day it complied` IS A DATE @desc The day it did so (any day if it has not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Compliance answer`
`Has the institution identified its associated trusts in time` MEANS
    `the compliance answer for the order of` `the day of the order` `within` (`the period ordered` `the court set another period` `the days the court set`) `complied` `it has complied` `on` `the day it complied` `as of` `today`

§§ `An earlier settlement (Part 7B)`

-- Situation: you settled your claim, or signed a release, before the law changed (before 1 February 2019 when a
-- limitation period had expired, or before 1 August 2022 when no one could be sued).

@export Is the settlement or release I agreed to an "affected agreement" that a court can set aside (Civil Liability Act 1936 (SA) s 50V)?
GIVEN `my age when abused` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in completed years when the abuse happened ("child" means under 18)
      `the kind of abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse` @desc The kind of abuse: sexual abuse; serious physical abuse; psychological abuse related to sexual abuse or serious physical abuse; physical abuse that was not serious; psychological abuse not related to those; or another kind of abuse
      `the body was responsible for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an organisation or body (private or public) was responsible for you and provided an activity, program or service of a kind that gives a person an opportunity to have contact with a child (answer FALSE if the abuser had no such body behind them)
      `the body is a family` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the "body" is in fact a family
      `the abuser's connection` IS A `Connection with the institution` @desc How the abuser was connected with that body (as in the abuse claim question)
      `I was in its care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the abuse happened while you were under that body's care, supervision, control or authority
      `it is for personal injury or death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim is for damages relating to personal injury to you (or a death) resulting from the abuse
      `it stops me suing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement prevents you from commencing or continuing proceedings on the claim
      `the day of the agreement` IS A DATE @desc The day the agreement was made
      `my time had run out then` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when the agreement was made, a limitation period on the claim had expired (even if you could have asked a court to extend it)
      `no one could be sued then` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when the agreement was made, proceedings could not be commenced or maintained against any person or institution that would have been liable under Part 7A had it then been in force (for example because the institution was unincorporated and had no proper defendant)
GIVETH AN `Affected agreement answer`
`Is my earlier settlement an affected agreement` MEANS
    `the affected agreement answer for` (`the agreement facts from` `my age when abused` `the kind of abuse` `the body was responsible for me` `the body is a family` `the abuser's connection` `I was in its care` `it is for personal injury or death` `it stops me suing` `the day of the agreement` `my time had run out then` `no one could be sued then`)

@export Can the court set aside my earlier settlement or release, so that I can sue (Civil Liability Act 1936 (SA) ss 50V, 50W)?
GIVEN `my age when abused` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in completed years when the abuse happened ("child" means under 18)
      `the kind of abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse` @desc The kind of abuse: sexual abuse; serious physical abuse; psychological abuse related to sexual abuse or serious physical abuse; physical abuse that was not serious; psychological abuse not related to those; or another kind of abuse
      `the body was responsible for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an organisation or body (private or public) was responsible for you and provided an activity, program or service of a kind that gives a person an opportunity to have contact with a child
      `the body is a family` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the "body" is in fact a family
      `the abuser's connection` IS A `Connection with the institution` @desc How the abuser was connected with that body (as in the abuse claim question)
      `I was in its care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the abuse happened while you were under that body's care, supervision, control or authority
      `it is for personal injury or death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim is for damages relating to personal injury to you (or a death) resulting from the abuse
      `it stops me suing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement prevents you from commencing or continuing proceedings on the claim
      `the day of the agreement` IS A DATE @desc The day the agreement was made
      `my time had run out then` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when the agreement was made, a limitation period on the claim had expired (even if you could have asked a court to extend it)
      `no one could be sued then` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when the agreement was made, no person or institution that would have been liable under Part 7A could be sued
      `it is a redress release` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a deed of release you signed in accepting an offer under the National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse, or an agreement about an earlier payment that was taken into account in that offer
      `it is an insurance contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a contract of insurance
      `the just and reasonable finding` IS A `Court finding` @desc Where the court stands on whether it is just and reasonable to set the agreement aside (found that it is; found that it is not; or not decided or not yet asked)
GIVETH A `Set aside answer`
`Can the court set aside my earlier settlement` MEANS
    `the set aside answer for` (`the agreement facts from` `my age when abused` `the kind of abuse` `the body was responsible for me` `the body is a family` `the abuser's connection` `I was in its care` `it is for personal injury or death` `it stops me suing` `the day of the agreement` `my time had run out then` `no one could be sued then`) `redress release` `it is a redress release` `insurance` `it is an insurance contract` `finding` `the just and reasonable finding`

@export If the court sets my earlier settlement aside, must I pay back what I received under it (Civil Liability Act 1936 (SA) s 50X)?
GIVEN `it has been set aside` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has set the agreement aside under Part 7B
GIVETH A `Repayment answer`
`Must I pay back what I received under the settlement` MEANS
    `the repayment answer` `it has been set aside`

-- Builds the agreement facts from the plain answers (not exported).
GIVEN `my age when abused` IS A NUMBER
      `the kind of abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse`
      `the body was responsible for me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a family` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the abuser's connection` IS A `Connection with the institution`
      `I was in its care` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is for personal injury or death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it stops me suing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the agreement` IS A DATE
      `my time had run out then` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no one could be sued then` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Agreement facts`
`the agreement facts from` `my age when abused` `the kind of abuse` `the body was responsible for me` `the body is a family` `the abuser's connection` `I was in its care` `it is for personal injury or death` `it stops me suing` `the day of the agreement` `my time had run out then` `no one could be sued then` MEANS
    `Agreement facts` WITH
        `the abuse facts` IS (`Abuse facts` WITH
            `the age when abused` IS `my age when abused`
            `the abuse` IS `the kind of abuse`
            `the body was responsible for the child and gave contact with children` IS `the body was responsible for me`
            `the body is a family` IS `the body is a family`
            `the abuser's connection` IS `the abuser's connection`
            `the child was under its care, supervision, control or authority` IS `I was in its care`)
        `the claim is for damages for personal injury or death` IS `it is for personal injury or death`
        `the agreement prevents proceedings on the claim` IS `it stops me suing`
        `the day of the agreement` IS `the day of the agreement`
        `a limitation period had expired then` IS `my time had run out then`
        `no one liable under Part 7A could then be sued` IS `no one could be sued then`
